  "cited_article_id": "configure-portal-result-visibility",
  "reply": "To set a delay, open **Settings > Patient Portal > Result Rules**, click **Add Rule**, choose the lab category (e.g., Pathology), and enter the number of hours in the **Hold Period** field. Turn on **Auto-Release** and save. The Hold Period timer is the delay before results appear in the portal (max 168 hours). Critical‑flagged results ignore the timer and require manual sign‑off. If results don’t show after the timer expires, check **Reports > Portal Log** for errors and ensure the patient has an active portal account."
}
